      <title>Hadoop Pig: Mapping &amp; reducing the easy way</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Data Analytics devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pig is a map/reduce query, or data flow language for use with Hadoop.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pig is a map/reduce query, or data flow language for use with Hadoop. In this talk I want to give a introduction to Pig, by example. What it&amp;#39;s for and how it&amp;#39;s used, I will focus on practice, more than theory, and will share our experiences with Hadoop and Pig at Netlog.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The presentation is focused at people who are new to Hadoop &amp;amp; Pig.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2561">Nathan Bijnens</person>
      </persons>
